Now all four dispatched.

We should verify that after each step the preconditions hold.

We need to ensure that after we release operator from origin, we still have operator available for destination etc. Yes.

Now check that we didn't miss any needed preconditions like candidate_operator_linked for lock_origin_availability etc. We assigned operator before lock, good.

Check that we didn't accidentally have candidate_operator_linked still attached when we detach task profile; that's fine.

Now we need to ensure that after we detach task profile from origin (step8), we still have candidate_operator_linked (yes) and origin_availability_locked (yes) etc.

Now after we reattach task profile to origin (step17), we need candidate_prepared still true? Yes, we haven't changed that.

Now after we attach service window to schedule candidates, we need candidate_clearance_established and route_sequence_context_set true (we have after establish_clearance_nominal). Good.

Now validate_route_sequence requires candidate_origin_availability_linked and candidate_destination_availability_linked; those are set in init for both shift candidates and never changed.

Now we need to ensure origin_availability_confirmed and destination_availability_confirmed remain true; they are set via lock actions and not changed.

Now we need to ensure that transport_leg_assembled and transport_leg_loading_authorized remain true; we never have actions that unset them. There's no action to disassemble or unauthorize. So they stay true.

Now we need to ensure that loading_container_leg_linked remains true for each container after loading; we load each container onto leg; after loading first container, loading_container_leg_linked true for lcA; after loading second container, also true for lcB. Both can be true simultaneously; no negative effect.

Now we need to ensure that loading_container_loaded is true for each container after loading; verify_loading_profile_nominal does not require loading_container_loaded; it's okay.

Now stage_schedule_candidate requires loading_container_loaded and loading_container_leg_linked (both true). Good.

Now verify_loading_profile_nominal requires loading_container_leg_linked (true) and not destination_leg_loaded (true) and not candidate_loading_verified (before verify). After we stage, candidate_staged_for_loading becomes true. Then verify requires not candidate_loading_verified (true). Good.

Now after verify, candidate_loading_verified becomes true.

Now establish_clearance_nominal requires candidate_loading_verified (true), candidate_compliance_certificate_linked (true), candidate_loading_container_linked (true), loading_container_leg_linked (true), not origin_leg_loaded (true), not destination_leg_loaded (true), not candidate_clearance_established (true). Good.

After establish, candidate_clearance_established true, route_sequence_context_set true.

Now attach_service_window requires candidate_clearance_established, route_sequence_context_set, service_window_available. Good.

Now validate_route_sequence requires candidate_service_window_linked (we just attached), candidate_task_profile_linked (still attached), origin_availability_confirmed, destination_availability_confirmed, not route_sequence_validated (false before). Good.

After validate, route_sequence_validated true.

Now finalize_candidate_after_sequence_validation requires candidate_clearance_established, route_sequence_validated, not candidate_finalized. Good.

After finalize, candidate_finalized true, dispatch_ready true.

Now allocate_dispatch_slot_for_candidate requires dispatch_ready true, candidate_task_profile_linked true, dispatch_slot_available true, not dispatch_allocated. All good.

Now execute_schedule_dispatch requires dispatch_allocated true, candidate_vehicle_linked true, candidate_dispatch_slot_linked true, not dispatched true. Good.

Now after execute, vehicle becomes available, dispatch_slot available.

Now we release operator, skill certificate, detach task profile.

Now we need to ensure that after we release skill certificate, we still have candidate_skill_certificate_linked? The release action removes it. That's fine.

Now we need to ensure that after we detach task profile, candidate_task_profile_linked becomes false; but we don't need it further.

Now we need to ensure that after we release operator, candidate_operator_linked becomes false; fine.

Now we need to ensure that after we release compliance certificate, candidate_compliance_certificate_linked becomes false; but we already used it for clearance; after finalize we don't need it.

Now we need to ensure that we didn't inadvertently leave any negative precondition violated later.

Now we need to double-check that we didn't forget to set candidate_prepared for schedule candidates; we did confirm_candidate_preparedness.

Now we need to ensure that we didn't forget to set candidate_vehicle_linked; we allocated vehicle.

Now we need to ensure that we didn't forget to set candidate_operator_linked for schedule candidates; we assigned operator.

Now we need to ensure that we didn't forget to set candidate_skill_certificate_linked; we assigned.

Now we need to ensure that we didn't forget to set candidate_compliance_certificate_linked; we assigned.

Now we need to ensure that we didn't forget to set candidate_loading_container_linked; it's already true from init.

Now we need to ensure that we didn't forget to set loading_container_leg_linked; we loaded container onto leg.

Now we need to ensure that we didn't forget to set loading_container_loaded; we loaded container.

Now we need to ensure that we didn't forget to set candidate_staged_for_loading; we staged.

Now we need to ensure that we didn't forget to set candidate_loading_verified; we verified.

Now we need to ensure that we didn't forget to set candidate_clearance_established; we established.

Now we need to ensure that we didn't forget to set route_sequence_context_set; we established.

Now we need to ensure that we didn't forget to set service_window_linked; we attached.

Now we need to ensure that we didn't forget to set route_sequence_validated; we validated.

Now we need to ensure that we didn't forget to set candidate_finalized; we finalized.

Now we need to ensure that we didn't forget to set dispatch_ready; finalize sets it.

Now we need to ensure that we didn't forget to set dispatch_allocated; we allocated.

Now we need to ensure that we didn't forget to set candidate_dispatch_slot_linked; allocate sets.

Now we need to ensure that we didn't forget to set dispatched; execute sets.

Now we need to ensure that we didn't inadvertently leave any negative predicate true that should be false for later steps.

For example, after we allocate dispatch slot for a candidate, dispatch_slot_available becomes false. After execute, it becomes true again.

